<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Everite yr shr dives, div falls.</title>
<headline>Everite yr shr dives, div falls.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     1.8	   vs   35.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 3.0	   vs    8.0</p>
<p>    Attrib profit	   1.62	  vs   31.28</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   5.58	  vs   43.51</p>
<p>    Tax			 3.22	  vs   11.99</p>
<p>    Turnover		547.47	  vs  619.67</p>
<p>Div payable: October 11</p>
<p>On register: September 27</p>
<p>Full name: Everite Group Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said earlier-than-expected global competition, closure costs of discontinued operations and the dumping of cheap goods in South Africa cut earnings by 95 percent to 1.8 cents per share.</p>
<p>However, the group expected the improved earnings trend of June 1995 to be resumed in the new financial year.</p>
<p>It said it was closing down loss-making businesses Santar, SFM and NSE and selling Tiger Tiles, a process which should be completed by the first quarter of the 1997 financial year.</p>
<p>It also said it was increasing its focus on management development throughout the group.</p>
<p>Future growth was expected to come from adding new product lines to existing businesses, expanding markets, growth in the water business and through acquisitions.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
